{
  "title": "Insta360 GO Ultra latch mount with TPU cage",
  "summary": "An all-purpose mount for the GO Ultra in its Action Pod: two printed hooks click into the pod's own latch slots (like Insta360's mount), a TPU cage glued to the base is a second hold in every direction and a bumper, and GoPro-standard prongs underneath take helmet, chest and bike mounts or the cold-shoe adapter.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-26",
  "material": "PLA now (PETG later for cold/impact action use): base, prongs, mount hardware on TNT. TPU 95A: cage and sponge on Gås. Bought: one M5 x 25-30 hex bolt + M5 nut.",
  "notes": "Three layers of holding. 1) Latch: two hooks on PLA spring arms printed in one piece with the base catch under the outer rims of the pod's latch slots; squeeze both end buttons to release (1.8 mm travel, hard stop, 1.3 % strain). A TPU sponge pushes the pod up against the catches (no rattle for a catch depth 0.9-2.4 mm). 2) TPU cage, glued to the base: posts at all four corners, a 1.3 mm wall behind the strip of body under the screen, a lip behind the grip-end strip (above the lanyard slot), a lip at the camera end's bottom corner, front lips at both ends, caps over the grip end's top-back corner and the camera's top corner. With the hooks removed it still stops the pod moving in every direction (verify_mount.py, A2). Nothing touches the screen panel or its flip path, the shutter, power, Q, USB-C (with a plug in), release slider, speaker, lens or lights. 3) Safety cord: an eyelet on the cage behind the grip end's bottom corner for the included cord through the pod's lanyard; use it on a helmet. GoPro-standard 2 prongs (2.9 mm, 3.3 gap, 5.4 hole) fit real GoPro mounts; with the cold-shoe foot, lock wheel and 3-prong head it goes on a camera or the Kinect rig. The joint uses a real M5 x 25-30 hex bolt (head glued into the printed knob) and a real M5 nut in the head's pocket: printed M5 threads are too fine (tested). Not knowable without the camera: latch hole depth (hooks reach 3.3 mm in), and the photo-scaled positions (+-0.6 mm on the slots, +-1-2 mm on the cage). Every cage feature that relies on a guess is TPU and can be trimmed with a knife. In PLA the hooks have a factor 1.4 at 10 g and the prongs are near their limit: fine for rigs and handheld; print in PETG for action use. Plates: TNT, PLA 230 C / 12 mm3/s, 1 h 49 min, 26 g, no supports. Gås, TPU cage 1 h 2 min, 6 g, 4 mm brim. Gås, TPU sponge 5 min (1 wall, 20 % gyroid). Assembly: superglue the sponge (top pocket), the prong block (bottom pocket) and the cage feet (base faces).",
